********************************************************************************
                                 IPIDE NOTES

==================================== BUGS ======================================

1. On a blank edit, you cannot move off line 1 until you type something.

2. When hitting line down from the starting screen, when the scroll takes
place, the scrollbar jumps. I suspect that the scroll position is set
from the cursor and not the top of page as should be.

3. The horizontal scrollbar does nothing.

4. Most of the FX keys do nothing.

5. Clicking on areas outside the text window removes the cursor and focus
from the text window. This problem needs gralib help to solve, either to
reject focus from areas that shouldn't have it, or a specific command to
direct focus to a given window.

6. Moving the cursor to mid screen, then hitting page down, then page up
several times results in the vertical slider unable to return to top. This
is likely because the check in page up for "already at top screen, go to top"
does not sync the slider position.

7. There is lots of tabbar flashes on redraws/resize. This seems to be
a feature of tabbars in Windows.

8. The tabbars are getting their stacking order flipped by a resize. This is
a longstanding issue with gralib/windows, and we may have to force widget
stacking order on such events.

9. For consistency with the "virtual space" model, we can remove the limit
on moving down into blank space. The scroll slider will simply remain at max
for these excursions.

=================================== Enhancements ===============================

1. Block copy, paste, move, in line and collumar mode.

2. Have a zone at line start that clicked, selects whole line.

3. Undo/redo.

4. Macros (goes with undo/redo).

5. Search, search/replace.

6. Toolbars.

7. Multiple split windows for views.

8. Help.

9. Save and restore previous position of window, and files and views being
worked on.

10. Implement regular expression searches and search/replace.

11. Add an options page to menu.

12. Add scanner or parser/scanner.

13. Color code program text.

14. Automatically load (or virtually load) all parts of a project.

15. Have the right side tabs actually come from source scans, or
disappear if document is not a Pascal source.

16. Have a bottom tab that lists extention types of the present name.

17. Ability to run compile/link/run from the interface, and capture error
files.

18. A cli command interface and language.

19. Have undo/redo present actions in cli form.

20. Ability to edit a graphical layout sheet, and generate a
program section to perform that layout.

21. Generate a left line that presents change bars from previous
(backup) version of document.

22. Allow right clicks on symbols in document to bring down
cross references and other info.

23. Tear off windows, menus and other items.

24. Version control.

25. Tree listing with its own window.

26. Ability to change keyword languages on the fly.

27. Ability to handle a bug tracking db for files, including
separate window, priority sorting, etc.